+## Local harness (ron-skills overlay)
+
+These lines override the rest of this skill and its playbooks on this machine.
+
+- **Repo rules win.** The repo's `AGENTS.md` and adapter docs outrank any pstack step, including language: user-visible text, comments, commit messages, and tracker notes follow the repo's language rule. **Writing the reply** and **Comments** apply only where they do not conflict.
+- **Forge.** There are no GitHub PRs. A delivery unit is a local branch with a candidate commit; "PR", "stack", "merge-ready", and "land" map to the repo adapter's candidate, batch branch, regression, and local merge into the integration branch. Pushing is the operator's, so never push. Skip `gh`, `origin`, `watch-pr`, Babysit, Shipping, and Opening a PR.
+- **No cloud.** A worker that would be `environment: "cloud"` runs locally as one Orca terminal session per unit in its own worktree, dispatched by the repo's tooling. Docker test runs share the machine, so respect the concurrency cap in the standing orders.
+- **Models.** Subagents are Claude models only; set the `effort` option instead of slug suffixes. The cross-family verifier is Codex through the repo's review script; when it fails, fall back to the `code-review` skill and record that verdict as lower-grade.
+- **Not installed.** `how`, `why`, `architect`, `arena`, `interrogate`, `swarm`, `teach`, `no-comments`, `technical-writing`, `figure-it-out`, `reflect`, `recall`, `deslop`, and `setup-pstack` are not linked, and pstack's `tdd` is replaced by Matt's. Where a trigger names a missing skill, use the Matt equivalent (`grilling`, `codebase-design`, `tdd`, `code-review`, `diagnosing-bugs`) or skip it with a one-line reason. Do not install or run `scripts/` (bun, orch store, watch-pr).
 
